            <div xml:id="d1195">

                <pb facs="1437" n="1423" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/2–1545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-15T20:00:00-04:00">February 15,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. It is not clear from your recent telegrams what action Venezuela
                    contemplates with respect to entering into a state of war or belligerency.
                    However, the Foreign Office should understand that before Escalante can sign the
                    United Nations Declaration we must have a Venezuelan communication to the effect
                    that Venezuela is “at war.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
